<PageLayout title="How Inqreon checks a page" description="Where prices come from, how a check is dated, and how to send a correction." h1="How we check">
  <h2>Sources</h2>
  <p>Prices, limits, and access rules come from the service’s own pages: pricing, help, supported-country lists, and terms. A news story or a blog is only a hint about where to look. A fact we have not confirmed is marked that way.</p>
  <h2>The date</h2>
  <p>A guide names the day it was last checked. When a price or a rule changes, the page and the date change with it.</p>
  <h2>Corrections</h2>
  <p>If something is wrong, write via <a href="/en/contact/">contact</a>. We recheck and correct it.</p>
  <h2>Ads</h2>
  <p>An affiliate link does not change what a guide concludes. It sits in a labeled block. See the <a href="/en/affiliates/">affiliate disclosure</a>.</p>
</PageLayout>
